    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0337" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v25/pg307"/>

                <head>122. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in the United Kingdom<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d122-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1956-10-26">October 26, 1956</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>3008. For Ambassador from Secretary. Please advise Selwyn Lloyd personally from me that developments in Hungary up
                    to moment increasingly suggest desirability of inscription of matter on Security
                    Council agenda. The revolt is assuming proportions which may in turn bring Red
                    counter-action of major proportions. Emotional reaction to this would be very
                    serious certainly in this country. It seems to me of great importance we should
                    promptly focus UN attention on this situation and
                    at same time obtain opportunity of informal talk with Soviet Permanent
                    Representative which might lead to an alleviation of situation which is
                    beginning to assume major dangerous implications.</p>
                <p>Would appreciate if possible reply by 10:00 a.m our time EDST Saturday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d122-f2"/> as I am meeting with
                    President on this matter at 11:00.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d122-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
